{title: I Am Determined To Hold Out}
{key: C}

{comment: Chorus}
[C]I am determined to hold out to the end,
[D]Jesus is with me, on [G]Him I can depend;
And I [C]know I have salvation, for I feel it in my [Am]soul;
[C]I am determined to [G]hold out to the [C]end.

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]When I first found Jesus, [F]something o'er me [C]stole,
Like [F]lightning it went through me, and glory filled my [G]soul;
Sal[C]vation made me happy, and [F]took my fears a[C]way,
And [F]when I meet old Satan, to [C]him I always [G]say:

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]Satan, was so angry, he [F]said he'd soon be [C]back:
Just [F]let the path get narrow, and he will lose the [G]track;
But [C]I'm so full of glory, my [F]Lord I always [C]find,
And [F]I just say to Satan, Old [C]man, get thee [G]behind.

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]This old-time religion [F]makes me sometimes [C]shout,
I [F]don't have time to gossip, nor any time to [G]pout;
They [C]say that I'm too noisy, [F]but when these blessings [C]flow,
I [F]shout, O hallelujah, I [C]want the world to [G]know.

{comment: Verse 4}
[C]When I hear the trumpet [F]sounding in the [C]sky,
And [F]see the mountains trembling, to Heaven I will [G]fly;
For [C]Jesus will be calling, [F]there'll be no time to [C]mend,
With [F]joy I'll go up singing, I've [C]held out to the [G]end.
